                <pb facs="0586" n="526" xml:id="pg526"/>

                <head>General Corona to Commander Bridges.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">MEXICAN REPUBLIC, FOURTH MILITARY DIVISION,
                        GENERAL-IN-CHIEF.</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Señor Commandante</hi>: I have the honor to
                    acknowledge to you the receipt of your communication No. 2, dated to-day.</p>
                <p>Having informed myself of its contents, I have again taken into consideration
                    your No. 1, received yesterday, and my reply to the same; but not finding
                    reasons for a change of opinion, I have to insist that the affair pertains to
                    the jurisdiction of the federal tribunals, in conformity with the laws of the
                    country, as it treats of an infraction of the fiscal regulations with reference
                    to the export of money.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to repeat to you the assurance of my consideration.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Independence and liberty! Headquarters in
                            <placeName>Mazatlan</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1868-06-18">June 18, 1868</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>R. CORONA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Commander</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">of her Britannic Majesty’s man-of-war Chanticleer,
                            anchored in the bay of this port.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
